From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 151/488] soh: rename func_800DF1D8 ->
 AudioHeap_ComputeRecurrences

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: computes two exponential recurrences into out[0..7] and out[8..15], per the in-tree comment. Unused (no callers) and carries a known @bug writing to out[] instead of tmp[], so its intended purpose is genuinely unknown -- the name describes only the arithmetic.
Defined in soh/src/code/audio_heap.c.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 soh/src/code/audio_heap.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/audio_heap.c b/soh/src/code/audio_heap.c
index 759d2dac4..00669384a 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/audio_heap.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/audio_heap.c
@@ -621,7 +621,8 @@ void* AudioHeap_SearchRegularCaches(s32 tableType, s32 cache, s32 id) {
     return NULL;
 }
 
-void func_800DF1D8(f32 p, f32 q, u16* out) {
+// LLM generated name (GUESS), was func_800DF1D8: computes two exponential recurrences into out[0..7] and out[8..15], per the in-tree comment. Unused (no callers) and carries a known @bug writing to out[] instead of tmp[], so its intended purpose is genuinely unknown -- the name describes only the arithmetic.
+void AudioHeap_ComputeRecurrences(f32 p, f32 q, u16* out) {
     // With the bug below fixed, this mysterious unused function computes two recurrences
     // out[0..7] = a_i, out[8..15] = b_i, where
     // a_{-2} = b_{-1} = 262159 = 2^18 + 15
